OL,3,GNEWSABlue plaque unveiled at ex-England
OL,4,Astriker's home                         
OL,6,FThe childhood home of former England   
OL,7,Fstriker Frank Worthington has been     
OL,8,Fhonoured with a blue plaque, on what   
OL,9,Fwould have been his 78th birthday.     
OL,11,FWorthington, who began his career at   
OL,12,FHuddersfield Town before playing for   
OL,13,FLeicester City, Bolton Wanderers and   
OL,14,FLeeds United, was born and raised in   
OL,15,Fthe terraced house on West Street in   
OL,16,FShelf, Halifax.                        
OL,18,FDuring his career he won eight caps for
OL,19,FEngland and was described by former    
OL,20,Fmanager Joe Mercer as "one of the best 
OL,21,Fcentre-forwards of all time".          
